# Dependencies deliberately removed from the root package.json.
#
# Upstream VS Code still declares these, so every upstream merge tries to
# restore them. A restored entry is easy to miss in a merge diff and can be
# silently harmful: `deemon` was re-added by the 1.130.0 merge alongside its
# replacement `@softwarenerd/deemon-ng`, and because both packages own the
# `deemon` bin name, npm resolved the collision differently in different
# checkouts of the same repo (see #15670).
#
# Listing a package here makes hygiene fail if it reappears in the root
# package.json `dependencies` or `devDependencies`. When resolving a
# package.json conflict during an upstream merge, keep Positron's removal.
#
# To intentionally reintroduce a package, delete its line here in the same
# commit and say why in the PR.

# Replaced by @softwarenerd/deemon-ng in #15264. Both packages provide a bin
# named `deemon`, so having both installed makes `npx deemon` resolve
# nondeterministically per install.
deemon
